-- story.0090: agent_credentials and payer_bindings, mirroring node-template 0039/0040 (credentials) and 0046 (payer bindings). Orgs (0045) are NOT adopted.
-- Generated by drizzle-kit from this node's schema, then made ADOPT-SAFE by hand (every object is created only when absent). The hand-written tail is what Drizzle cannot emit.
--
-- WHY ADOPT-SAFE (evidence, read-only, 2026-11-26). The red candidate-a database (cogni_red) already holds agent_credentials, from a reverted flight:
--   - Origin: red#67 (story.5158, @cogni-dao/agent-grants 0.5.0), migration 0034_agent_authority (journal when 1794530229376, 2026-11-12), merged to main 2026-11-13 06:04Z and reverted
--     08:04Z (#70). Its migrations 0034 to 0037 ran on candidate-a and left four ledger rows Red's journal does not know (Loki COGNI_MIGRATION_RECEIPT_V1 shows them as
--     `unknown:1794530255664`, `unknown:1794546548368`, `unknown:1794546559637` and one more; hashes e7f6f2dc..., 73aaa443..., 3f34b207...).
--   - Data: 6 agent_credentials rows (2d8bdf13, d4590770, d71021fb, 97de535b, 24faf2f9, 9e32efb8), key_upgrade / rotation validation runs issued 2026-11-13 05:38 and 06:03 UTC for three
--     agents that all exist in users. Zero orphans; every foreign key is validated; columns, constraints and indexes equal this file's definition.
--   - The earlier "orphan rows" diagnosis was PHANTOM: users has FORCE RLS (self_isolation: id = app.current_user_id) and a migration batch is one transaction, so the 0035 seed leaves a
--     transaction-local app.current_user_id; the owner role then sees ONE users row and every credential looks orphaned (the old re-add of the users foreign key failed with that
--     exact error, and a DELETE on that predicate would have removed all six real rows; both patches were reverted). Reproduced on a scratch Postgres.
--   - Production never ran red#67: its Red migration receipts show declared == applied through 0034_legal_vivisector, with no unknown ledger row. On production every object below is created.
-- RULES OF THIS FILE: no DELETE, no UPDATE, no DROP; an existing table must already have the expected shape (asserted, else the migration fails loudly); constraints, indexes, functions and
-- the trigger are added only when absent; the users foreign key is never dropped or re-added.
--
-- Role handling matches 0035: act as the non-bypass owner of public.users, so the new tables belong to the same owner whether this runs
-- alone or after 0035 in one transaction.
DO $$
DECLARE owner_name text;
BEGIN
  SELECT r.rolname INTO owner_name FROM pg_class c JOIN pg_roles r ON r.oid = c.relowner
  WHERE c.oid = 'public.users'::regclass AND NOT r.rolsuper AND NOT r.rolbypassrls;
  IF owner_name IS NULL OR NOT pg_has_role(current_user, owner_name, 'MEMBER') THEN
    RAISE EXCEPTION 'identity adoption requires membership in the non-bypass users owner';
  END IF;
  EXECUTE format('SET LOCAL ROLE %I', owner_name);
END $$;
--> statement-breakpoint
-- Session-local helpers, in the same migration transaction (not application runtime DDL).
CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION pg_temp.add_constraint_if_absent(tab text, cname text, ddl text)
RETURNS void LANGUAGE plpgsql AS $f$
BEGIN
  IF NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM pg_constraint WHERE conrelid = to_regclass('public.' || tab) AND conname = cname) THEN
    EXECUTE ddl;
  END IF;
END
$f$;
